\paragraph{List decodability of RS codes.}
While \emph{folded} RS codes have been shown to achieve the list decoding capacity in  \cite{GR08}, understanding the list decodability of RS codes remains an important problem and has attracted a lot of attention. See, e.g., \cite{guruswami2004list, rudra2007list, vadhan2012pseudorandomness}. By the classical \emph{Johnson bound} \cite{Johnson1962new, GS01}, an RS code of rate $R$ is list decodable up to the radius  around $1-\sqrt{R}$.
