If $X$ is a totally ordered finite set, we define the inside-ranking function $\pi$ as
\[
\pi(X) := (r_1, \ldots, r_{|X|}),
\]
where $\{r_1, \ldots, r_{|X|}\} = \{1, \ldots, |X|\}$ and for any $1 \leq i \leq |X|$, $r_i$ is the rank of $x_i$ inside $X$.
