\textbf{RQ2} aims to investigate how English linguists experts vs. 
English linguists non-experts detect deepfake texts. 
The hypothesis is that experts will focus more on high-level errors such as logical fallacies and experts will focus more on low-level errors such as grammar issues. \textit{CITE} states that using grammar issues to detect deepfake texts is not advisable as humans make grammar issues as well. We find this statement to be true in our experiments as well. 
\textbf{RQ3} aims to investigate the factors that improve human performance in deepfake text detection. Whether is it the errors that experts focus on or the collaboration approach, either asynchronous or synchronous.


