If $A_{u,v}(\mathfrak{b},\mathfrak{c}) = \mathbf{1}\{\mathfrak{b} \neq \mathfrak{c}\}$ for every edge $(u,v)$ (forbidding monochromatic edges) and $\lambda_v(\mathfrak{c}) = 1$ for every vertex $v$ (no external fields\/no biases towards colors), then we get the uniform distribution over all proper list colorings of $G$. 
