\begin{theorem}\label{main}
Let $R$ be a complete discrete valuation ring in mixed characteristic with residue field of characteristic $p$, let $G$ be a finite $p$-group and let $U$ be a pseudocompact $RG$-lattice.  Suppose there is a normal subgroup $N$ of $G$  such that
\begin{itemize}
\item the module $U$ restricted to $N$ is a free $RN$-module,
\item the submodule of fixed points $U^N$ is a permutation $RG$-module.
\end{itemize}
Then $U$ itself is a permutation $RG$-module.
\end{theorem}


